From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:48:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 303/342] freebsd_network: m_free() deletes the tags of all
 packet headers

FreeBSD's mbuf zone destructor deletes an mbuf's tags, so m_free() itself
only does it for M_NOFREE ones, which never reach the zone. There's no such
destructor here, so all the other tags stayed allocated.

net80211 tags each received frame with its receive parameters: about 42 MB
per GB downloaded, and a board at full Wi-Fi load ran out of memory in 74
minutes. KDL showed 7 million of them in the 256 byte block allocator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/mbuf.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/mbuf.c b/src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/mbuf.c
index c0d9ae2bfd..bd2dc432d0 100644
--- a/src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/mbuf.c
+++ b/src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/mbuf.c
@@ -309,7 +309,9 @@ m_free(struct mbuf* memoryBuffer)
 {
 	struct mbuf* next = memoryBuffer->m_next;
 
-	if ((memoryBuffer->m_flags & (M_PKTHDR|M_NOFREE)) == (M_PKTHDR|M_NOFREE))
+	// FreeBSD's mbuf zone does this for all but the M_NOFREE ones when they're
+	// freed; there's no such zone here, and a wireless driver tags each frame.
+	if ((memoryBuffer->m_flags & M_PKTHDR) != 0)
 		m_tag_delete_chain(memoryBuffer, NULL);
 	if (memoryBuffer->m_flags & M_EXT)
 		mb_free_ext(memoryBuffer);
